{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q015_artifact_tag_not_homology\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, d1a14h2 is the 1a14 chain H residues 1-8 segment classified as an artificial N-terminal tag: class l “Artifacts”, fold/superfamily/family l.1/l.1.1/l.1.1.1 “Tags”, protein “N-terminal Tags”, species “Synthetic”. It should not be treated as biological protein homology evidence; SCOPe explicitly marks homology as not implied for this artifact entry and warns that class l records are artificial sequence artifacts whose similarity does not imply biological homology. The homologous antibody variable domain in this chain is d1a14h1, residues 9-111, in b.1.1.1 V set domains, so similarity to the 1-8 tag must not be transferred to the VH domain’s family, superfamily, fold, function, or template choice.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1/parents\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/parents\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/homology\"]}]}"}}
